Description: Jump Desktop
Author: Phill Moore
Version: 1.0
Id: d05c37c0-2dc5-4fe4-bed4-eb68e795255a
RecreateDirectories: true
Targets:
    -
        Name: Jump Desktop Viewer - User Configuration and Connection Database
        Category: Communications
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\AppData\Roaming\Jump Desktop\
        Recursive: true
        Comment: "Collects Jump Desktop Viewer (client) configuration, connection database (e.g. connection.db), and related per-user data"
    -
        Name: Jump Desktop Viewer - LocalAppData
        Category: Communications
        Path: C:\Users\%user%\AppData\Local\Jump Desktop\
        Recursive: true
        Comment: "Collects Jump Desktop Viewer local application data including any cached data and logs"
    -
        Name: Jump Desktop Connect - Configuration
        Category: Communications
        Path: C:\ProgramData\Jump Desktop\Connect\
        FileMask: '*.conf'
        Comment: "Collects Jump Desktop Connect configuration files from ProgramData"
    -
        Name: Jump Desktop Connect - Logs
        Category: Communications
        Path: C:\ProgramData\Jump Desktop\Connect\Logs\
        Recursive: true
        Comment: "Collects Jump Desktop Connect service and diagnostic log files (e.g. service.log) from ProgramData"
    -
        Name: Jump Desktop Connect - ProgramData Root
        Category: Communications
        Path: C:\ProgramData\Jump Desktop\Connect\
        FileMask: '*.log'
        Comment: "Collects any log files stored directly in the Connect ProgramData folder"
    -
        Name: Jump Desktop Connect - Installed Logs
        Category: Communications
        Path: C:\Program Files\Jump Desktop\Connect\logs\
        Recursive: true
        Comment: "Collects Jump Desktop Connect logs from the installation directory (alternate location on some installs)"

# Documentation
# https://jumpdesktop.com/
# https://changelog.jumpdesktop.com/browser-connections-diagnostic-logs-and-sso-improvements-2YJQxq
# https://support.jumpdesktop.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/214915623-Activity-Log
# https://support.jumpdesktop.com/hc/en-us/articles/360049783711-How-do-I-send-logs-from-Jump-Desktop-Connect-
# https://jumpdesktop.com/support/docs/windows/connect/faq/how-to-find-connect-log-files/
# Jump Desktop is a remote desktop (RDP/VNC/Fluid) client and server suite. The Windows product line has two components:
#   * Jump Desktop (Viewer/Client) - stores per-user configuration and a connection database under %AppData%\Jump Desktop and %LocalAppData%\Jump Desktop.
#   * Jump Desktop Connect (Server/Agent) - runs as a service and stores configuration and diagnostic logs under %ProgramData%\Jump Desktop\Connect (with logs typically in the Logs subfolder, e.g. service.log). Team admins can remotely request these diagnostic logs from the Jump Desktop dashboard on Connect v10 beta 6 and later.
